Project uses **pnpm**. Run root scripts from the **repository root**.

Run `pnpm lint` (and fix what it reports) **before every commit**. Full verification policy: @buildcheck.mdc.

Under the hood (root `package.json`) both scripts cover **four** packages — `@meriter/api`, `@meriter/web`, `@meriter/community-web`, `@meriter/uzz-web`:

- `pnpm lint` — api runs eslint **with `--fix`** (may modify files); web, community-web and uzz-web are check-only.
- `pnpm lint:fix` — same api step, then `lint:fix` (eslint `--fix`) for the three web apps. Only those steps differ from `pnpm lint`.

Dev setup and per-OS commands: @local-dev-linux.mdc (canonical) or `docs/LOCAL_DEVELOPMENT_SETUP.md`.

### API tests and mongodb-memory-server

- API Jest runs use in-memory MongoDB; temp data lives under `api/.cache/mongo-mem-test`.
- `pretest` sweeps stale orphaned dirs before each `pnpm --filter @meriter/api test`.
- If `/tmp/mongo-mem-*` or cache dirs accumulate (e.g. after Ctrl+C): `pnpm test:cleanup-mongo` from the root (add `pnpm --filter @meriter/api test:cleanup-mongo -- --force` to kill live mongod).
- Tests that use multi-document transactions (e.g. merit transfer) need `MongoMemoryReplSet`, not a standalone server.
